        "created_at": "2015-01-17T18:53:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"EdgeDS\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n EdgeDS:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>phantaskippy wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Yeah, it cares what cards are in that players play area. &nbsp;It would update just like \"X\" updates.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nNot sure if this is something y'all discussed during playtesting, but the portion of UYITG that copies the other hero's ongoings - does anyone know for sure if that text on UYITG considered to be before or after the closing line on the base card to destroy it at the start of Guise's next turn? &nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It goes in the order on the card, so all copied start of turn text will happen before the destruction on Guise's turn. &nbsp;Of course any copied effect that destroys at the start of the turn will destroy Uh, Yeah.</p>",
